Seam: ChromeBrowserMainParts::Create, in chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc,
      where the macOS startup parts are added.
Why: the updater belongs to the browser process rather than to any window,
     and nothing of Arcium's ran once per process until now. Chromium's
     startup parts are the place such things join, and they are told when
     the browser has started and when its message loop has ended -- the two
     moments the updater needs: it starts once startup is over, and lets go
     of the settings store before that store is destroyed.
Delegates to: arcium/ui/browser/browser_updates.cc (arcium::BrowserUpdates).

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
index 21d499a926..fba1ae2ca9 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
@@ -224,6 +224,7 @@
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 #include <Security/Security.h>
 
+#include "arcium/ui/browser/browser_updates.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/mac/chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_mac.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/cocoa/keystone_infobar_delegate.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/ui_features.h"
@@ -804,6 +805,7 @@ std::unique_ptr<content::BrowserMainParts> ChromeBrowserMainParts::Create(
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
   main_parts->AddParts(std::make_unique<ChromeBrowserMainExtraPartsMac>());
+  main_parts->AddParts(std::make_unique<arcium::BrowserUpdates>());
 #endif
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
